cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Open Trust Commons (OTCS — Open Trust Coordination System)"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Perkins
    given-names: Chris
    alias: nmcitra
abstract: >-
  An open protocol and public registry for locating trust-related projects
  within a shared action-governance coordinate system; preserving their
  provenance, maturity, evidence and relationships; and enabling voluntary
  composition, testing and collaboration without requiring centralized
  ownership or manufactured consensus.
keywords:
  - trust
  - governance
  - agentic systems
  - provenance
  - registry
  - interoperability
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-trust-commons/otcs-registry"
# v0.1.0 is the first public release; nothing below it was ever published.
# `date-released` and `doi` are set when the release is actually cut
# (RELEASE-PROCESS.md §2) — a release date written in advance is a guess.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Kinetic Trust Protocol (KTP)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Perkins
        given-names: Chris
    notes: >-
      Independently authored. OTCS adopts KTP's coordinate system; OTCS does
      not own KTP. KTP is registered in this registry under the same evidence
      rules as every other project.
